--- opencode r
run 	run opencode with a message
--- opencode run --
--agent=	agent to use
--attach=	attach to a running opencode server (e.g., http://localhost:4096)
--auto 	auto-approve permissions that are not explicitly denied (dangerous!)
--command=	the command to run, use message for args
--continue 	continue the last session
--dir=	directory to run in, path on remote server if attaching
--file=	file(s) to attach to message
--fork 	fork the session when continuing (use with --continue or --session)
--format=	format: default (formatted) or json (raw JSON events)
--help 	show help
--interactive 	run in direct interactive split-footer mode
--log-level=	log level
--model=	model to use in the format of provider/model
--password=	
--port=	port for the local server (defaults to random port if no value provided)
--print-logs 	print logs to stderr
--pure 	run without external plugins
--session=	session id to continue
--share 	share the session
--thinking 	show thinking blocks
--title=	title for the session (uses truncated prompt if no value provided)
--username=	basic auth username (defaults to OPENCODE_SERVER_USERNAME or 'opencode')
--variant=	model variant (provider-specific reasoning effort, e.g., high, max, minimal)
--version 	show version number
